The School of Planning and Architecture Act, 2014
"Statutes" and "Ordinances", in relation to any School, means the Statutes and Ordinances of that School made under
this Act.
Chapter II
The Schools

28.
Statutes.
- Subject to the provisions of this Act, the Statutes may provide for all or any of the following matters, namely:-
(a)
the conferment of honorary degrees;
(b)
the formation of departments of teaching and centres for research;
(c)
the fees to be charged for courses of study in the School and for admission to the examinations of degrees and
diplomas of the School;
(d)
the institution of fellowship, scholarships, exhibitions, medals and prizes;
(e)
the term of office and the method of appointment of officers of the School;
(f)
the qualifications of teachers of the School;
(g)
the classification, the method of appointment and the determination of the terms and conditions of service of teachers
and other staff of the School;
(h)
the constitution of pension, insurance and provident funds for the benefit of the officers, teachers and other staff of the
School;
(i)
the constitution, powers and duties of the authorities of the School;
(j)
the establishment and maintenance of halls and hostels;
(k)
the conditions of residence of students of the School and the levying of fees for residence in the halls and hostels and of
other charges;
(l)
the allowances to be paid to the Chairperson and Members of the Board;
(m)
the authentication of the orders and decisions of the Board; and
(n)
the meetings of the Board, the Senate, or any Committee, the quorum at such meetings and the procedure to be
followed in the conduct of their business.
